From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Editor: use the window manager's title bar and border on Linux

The Editor wraps its main window in AzQtComponents::WindowDecorationWrapper
with OptionAutoTitleBarButtons everywhere except macOS, so on Linux O3DE
draws its own title bar and Qt asks the X11 window manager for no
decorations (_MOTIF_WM_HINTS decorations 0). The window manager then gives
the window no resize border. O3DE's own resize handling on Linux is only
4-pixel strips of its title bar (TitleBar::isTopResizeArea and friends; the
12-pixel border handler is Windows-only), and under XWayland on development
241c78b806 (2026-10-15) only the status bar's size grip in the lower right
corner resized the window. On GNOME under XWayland the main window
cannot be resized from its edges, and title bar drags never reach the
window manager, so tile-snap does not work either (o3de/o3de#19820).
Use OptionDisabled on Linux too, as on macOS: the window manager draws the
title bar and border and runs move, resize, maximize and snapping itself.
The window title already propagates in this mode (o3de/o3de#19750).

--- a/Code/Editor/CryEdit.cpp
+++ b/Code/Editor/CryEdit.cpp
@@ -1545,7 +1545,10 @@
     ((CCryDocManager*)m_pDocManager)->SetDefaultTemplate(pDocTemplate);
 
     auto mainWindow = new MainWindow();
-#ifdef Q_OS_MACOS
+    // On Linux, let the window manager draw the main window's title bar and border, as on macOS.
+    // With O3DE's own title bar the X11 window asks for no decorations, so the window manager gives
+    // it no resize border to drag.
+#if defined(Q_OS_MACOS) || defined(Q_OS_LINUX)
     auto mainWindowWrapper = new AzQtComponents::WindowDecorationWrapper(AzQtComponents::WindowDecorationWrapper::OptionDisabled);
 #else
     auto mainWindowWrapper = new AzQtComponents::WindowDecorationWrapper(AzQtComponents::WindowDecorationWrapper::OptionAutoTitleBarButtons);
